= 1 June 2025 — Poland chooses the Palace

Turnout: **[+ pres_2025_runoff_turnout +]%** ·
Valid votes: **[+ pres_2025_runoff_valid_votes_display +]**

**[+ pres_2025_runoff_a_name +] [+ pres_2025_runoff_a_share +]%**
([+ pres_2025_runoff_votes_a_display +])  
**[+ pres_2025_runoff_b_name +] [+ pres_2025_runoff_b_share +]%**
([+ pres_2025_runoff_votes_b_display +])

{!<div class="election-map-host" data-election-map-source="president-2025-r2"></div>!}

Margin: **[+ pres_2025_runoff_margin +] points**

President-elect: **[+ pres_2025_winner +]**.

The eliminated electorates did not transfer as party leaders instructed.
Lewica's line — **[+ pres_2025_transfer_strategy +]** — opened doors and moved
organisers; voters still decided whether to walk through them. The last
fortnight was spent on **[+ pres_2025_runoff_final_push +]**, and no campaign
will ever know what the other version of it would have produced.

Every camp will claim it supplied the decisive voters; the certified count
gives the presidential pen to one person for the next five years.

[? if pres_2025_winner_key = "left": Lewica has won the Palace. **[+
pres_2025_winner +]** must now become President of the Republic without turning
the office into party headquarters. [? if left_in_government: Our ministers
and caucus will be judged by whether a friendly signature produces actual
law.?][? if not left_in_government: Our caucus must prove that a Left president
can widen the party's reach without treating the Palace as an opposition
headquarters.?]?]
[? if pres_2025_winner_key = "razem": **[+ pres_2025_winner +]** reaches the
Palace through Razem's opposition campaign. The wider Left gains a president
and a new internal centre of gravity: New Left must work with a rival who can
sign its bills and publicly expose their compromises.?]
[? if pres_2025_winner_key = "ko": **[+ pres_2025_winner +]** gives the
democratic camp a friendlier Palace, but KO will own the victory. Lewica gains
a route around the veto wall for bills it can help pass; every democratic party
loses the excuse that presidential obstruction explains every undelivered
social promise.?]
[? if pres_2025_winner_key = "right": PiS-backed <span class="party-pis"><b>[+ pres_2025_right_candidate +]</b></span> wins the
Palace. [? if left_in_government: Lewica's ministers face five years in which
every labour, equality and court bill needs a bargain, an override the cabinet
does not possess, or a public veto campaign.?][? if not left_in_government:
Lewica must oppose both the cabinet and a President prepared to block the bills
it can assemble in the Sejm.?]?]
[? if pres_2025_winner_key = "mentzen": <span class="party-konf"><b>[+ pres_2025_konf_candidate +]</b></span> turns the
Konfederacja electorate into presidential power. Lewica must defend
public institutions against a hostile pen while PiS decides whether to follow
or compete with the new leader of the right.?]
[? if pres_2025_winner_key = "braun": <span class="party-korona"><b>Grzegorz Braun</b></span> carries his personal
far-right movement into the Palace. Minority organisations and public servants
now require institutional protection, and every unresolved legal proceeding
will be recast as a conflict involving the head of state.?]
[? if pres_2025_winner_key = "holownia": <span class="party-p2050"><b>[+ pres_2025_centre_candidate +]</b></span> converts a
centrist campaign into the presidency. Poland 2050 must learn to live without
its founder's daily command; Lewica gains an institutional partner who will
still compete for reformist and public-service voters.?]
[? if pres_2025_winner_key = "stanowski": Media entrepreneur **Krzysztof
Stanowski** has turned a campaign about political ritual into the presidency
itself. Every parliamentary party now faces an officeholder with an audience
but no settled party machine.?]

